1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,830
When a bank gives you a loan, it
doesn't lend you anyone's money.

2
00:00:04,850 --> 00:00:06,940
It types a number into your account.

3
00:00:07,110 --> 00:00:09,804
And that money just… exists.

4
00:00:09,824 --> 00:00:11,964
You've probably heard the other version.

5
00:00:11,984 --> 00:00:17,214
You deposit $10,000, the bank
keeps 10%, and lends out the rest.

6
00:00:17,234 --> 00:00:20,354
The Bank of England calls
that a misconception.

7
00:00:20,374 --> 00:00:25,603
In their words: whenever a bank makes
a loan, it creates a matching deposit.

8
00:00:25,623 --> 00:00:30,414
And that 10% rule? In America, the
reserve requirement has been zero since

9
00:00:30,434 --> 00:00:31,381
2020.

10
00:00:31,401 --> 00:00:34,261
So your loan doesn't come from savers.

11
00:00:34,281 --> 00:00:36,231
Your loan is the new money.

12
00:00:36,251 --> 00:00:40,071
That's why 97% of
Britain's money isn't cash.

13
00:00:40,091 --> 00:00:42,141
It's numbers in bank accounts.

14
00:00:42,161 --> 00:00:46,151
And here's the strangest part.
When you pay the loan back…

15
00:00:46,481 --> 00:00:48,675
the money is destroyed.

16
00:00:48,775 --> 00:00:52,945
It's not unlimited. Interest rates
and regulators keep it in check.

17
00:00:52,965 --> 00:00:54,985
But that money in your account?

18
00:00:55,115 --> 00:00:56,435
Someone owes it.
